  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/34145d4a924027964096df2eae6e87d31832833528aef06203a1b1f43f73d2ac.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=4.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{f(x)-f(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=2.$ Applying the above formula with $x=2$ and $h=4$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(2) & \u2248\\frac{f(2)-f(2-4)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2)-f(-2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-1}{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
